# K18 guard corpus — DEEP LOOP NESTING (docs/design/k18_memo_design.md §5
# item 12; docs/dev/known_issues.md K18, FIXED 2026-08-15).
#
# THE CORPUS TOPS OUT AT LOOP-NESTING DEPTH 4. That is why this file exists,
# and it guards a COST/RESOURCE class rather than an answer: the K18 repair
# keys the closure memo on the open-loop context, and the number of distinct
# contexts on nested nullable stars grows as d^2/2 — 31,627 contexts at 250,
# the deepest nesting the parser accepts (PCREC_MAX_GROUP_DEPTH,
# src/core/limits.h). The design's prototype descended once per context with a
# C stack frame, which measured 31,377 frames deep: ~7 MB of the default 8 MB
# stack on a plain build and an outright stack overflow under AddressSanitizer
# at nesting depth 210. Nothing in the suite went anywhere near it.
#
# The shipped repair makes clo_walk fully iterative (an explicit LIFO of
# deferred branches in the compile's arena), so C-stack depth no longer
# depends on the pattern at all. These blocks are what would notice if that
# ever regressed — under `make asan` they are the case that fails first, and
# under a plain build the 250-deep block is a compile-time canary (measured
# 0.37 s against the pre-K18 compiler's 0.004 s; the harness's own budget for
# a pcrec invocation is 60 s).
#
# The last two blocks are the axes the pure-nesting ladder does not cover: a
# LAZY inner quantifier at the same depth, and forty nullable loops in
# SEQUENCE rather than nested (a chain, which is what the pre-M2.8 recursive
# tail edges were made iterative for).
#
# THIS FILE IS ALSO THE GROW-PATH TEST the design note asked for on purpose
# (§5 item 7). The repair adds three arena-backed tables with doubling/rehash
# paths — the context interner, the (state, ctx) memo and the deferred-branch
# stack — and neither the corpus nor the fuzzer drives any of them past their
# initial capacity, which is how the design lane's first prototype shipped a
# table that HUNG rather than grew when full. The 250-deep blocks mint 31,627
# contexts and 64,768 expansions against initial capacities of 64 and 256, so
# every doubling path here runs many times over, and runs under `make asan`.
#
# Every expectation generated from python3 `re` AND libpcre2 10.46, both
# oracles agreeing on every cell (D44's three-way rule).

pattern (?:(?:(?:(?:a*)*)*)*)*
